==English==

===Etymology===
{{unk.}} origin. Perhaps from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|lang=fro|tremouille||the hopper of a mill}}.<!-- Webster 1913, Century 1911; also OEtD, which speaks of M.Fr. tremouille. -->

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtɜrmɔɪl/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# A state of great disorder or uncertainty.

====Synonyms====
